			[
				"Caveats",
				{
					"type": "rect",
					"cX": 1820,
					"cY": 1412.29296875,
					"rH": 260,
					"rV": 156,
					"radii": 6,
					"html": "Caveats — known trade-offs",
					"style": ";padding:10px 14px 8px 20px\n;font-size:12px\n;font-weight:700\n;letter-spacing:.04em\n;color:light-dark(#b45309,#fcd34d)\n;align-items:start"
				},
				{
					"fill": "none",
					"stroke": "#f59e0b",
					"lineWidth": 1.5,
					"lineDash": [
						4,
						3
					]
				}
			],
			[
				"Caveats Text",
				{
					"type": "rect",
					"cX": 1820,
					"cY": 1426.29296875,
					"rH": 244,
					"rV": 116,
					"html": "• Every login and read crosses the VPN — an on-prem outage stalls the whole portal ( tunnels are redundant, the site is not )<br>• Throughput is capped by the IdP and the Sanitized Reader<br>• Sanitization <i>is</i> the sovereignty guarantee — allowlist fields only; joins / aggregates can re-identify<br>• Caching sanitized data cloud-side would ease load, at the cost of the sovereignty claim<br>• Active-active holds only with: a neutral <b>dual-provider</b> GSLB ( DNS outages have repeatedly taken whole fleets down — Dyn 2016, Akamai 2021 ) or client-side fallback across clouds, each cloud sized for 100% of traffic, both stacks always hot, and no single-cloud dependencies ( payments, push, registry, monitoring )",
					"style": ";display:grid\n;place-items:start\n;padding:0 6px\n;font-size:11px\n;line-height:1.5\n;color:light-dark(#475569,#94a3b8)\n;text-align:left"
				},
